Hmm, wait — what does that mean? The atomaton server (in the real `atomaton` def) offers launch_sub_agent and request_close_issue; atomaton_env is the same program with an allowlist. The duplicate_tool check sees servers' tools... two servers claiming the same tool name? Since atomaton_env is the same program as atomaton with unprefixed names, both would advertise `request_close_issue` unprefixed — duplicate_tool check would flag it. But because atomaton_env has a tool_allowlist, the advertised set is narrowed... Hmm, but the comment says the duplicate check "would otherwise see this server claim a second time" — meaning the allowlist prevents the duplicate claim.

If I add `request_close_issue` to the allowlist, then does the duplicate_tool check now flag atomaton_env and atomaton both claiming `request_close_issue`? That depends on whether a server that an agent's definition doesn't use counts. The duplicate check is probably per-definition — checks the tools an agent gets from its named servers. An engineer's definition names `atomaton_env`, not `atomaton`, so there'd be no duplicate in the engineer's set. But wait — the atomaton agent definition names `atomaton`; engineer names `atomaton_env`; reviewer? Let me check the agent definitions and the duplicate_tool logic.

